Demucs (pretrained weights) — not MIT
-------------------------------------

Official pretrained checkpoints (`htdemucs`, `htdemucs_ft`, and related
bags) are **not** covered by the MIT license.

On 2022-05-23, Alexandre Défossez stated in
facebookresearch/demucs#327:

    The model weights are not covered by the MIT license, and are
    provided only for scientific purposes.

No later statement on the archived facebookresearch/demucs repo or the
adefossez/demucs fork retracts that. Training data includes MUSDB HQ
(research terms) and internal Meta recordings. Third-party re-hosts that
label the same checkpoints MIT or CC-BY-NC do not have authority to
relicense them.

Product policy (user decision, 2026-08-18)
------------------------------------------

- Development may download official Demucs weights (checksummed) into a
  local directory via `scripts/download_demucs.py`.
- The shipped product does **not** bundle official Demucs weights.
- The end user must click **Download model** before inference. Clicking
  is not a sublicense of the weights.
- Inference loads only a local `repo=` path. The engine must not
  auto-fetch from Hugging Face or Facebook public files when
  `Separator()` / a job runs without that click.

CI forbids `huggingface.co/adefossez` and `dl.fbaipublicfiles.com` in
engine load-path modules (`separate.py`, `models.py`, and other infer
paths) and in `host/`. Those strings are allowed in
`scripts/download_demucs.py`, `engine/perfectvoice_engine/weight_fetch.py`,
and `docs/`.


